  📋 Interview Drill — [TYPE: Technical-Flutter]
    Q: "In Flutter, when would you NOT change the URL of an already-indexed page?"
    Ans (memorize this):
      1. I had two Flutter lesson pages that were ranking in Google at positions 9 and 12.
      2. I wanted to add "Flutter" to the page title to match the search query better. But I saw the build script creates the file name from the title. If I change the title, the URL changes and the old URL gets a 404. Google loses the ranking signal.
      3. Instead I only changed the meta description field. The URL stayed the same. The ranking signals stayed safe.
    Example (in user's voice):
      "The page was already ranking in Google. The file name came from the title. If I changed the title, the URL would change and break. So I only changed the description — that is what shows in search results. The URL stayed the same and the ranking stayed safe."
    Why this works: shows I check how the system works before I make a change.
    🎯 Bonus follow-up the interviewer might ask: "What if you had to change the URL — what would you do to keep the SEO value?"
